    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "view.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Add has_folds on impl View. Keep it public. Do not add a dead_code attribute. The body is !self.folds.is_empty(). Do not nest an if inside an if.  Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch line_scalar, apply_indent_folds, or is_scrolled. The existing test apply_indent_folds_stores_char_ranges stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test a_new_view_has_no_folds builds a view the same way that test does. has_folds is false. After apply_indent_folds of a, newline, two spaces, b, newline with tab width 4, has_folds is true. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
  },
